  "body": "LOT-168\n\nCloses #286\n\nClaim: cloud/lot-168-sonnet\n\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/lot-168-sonnet)\n\n**Problem.** The REST completion (`RESTBrowsingClient.completingSubforums`, PR #928) and the `SubforumInjection` fallback were only checked against 3 captured categories (1, 2, 10). The entries for Photo numérique, Windows & Software, Graphisme and Achats & Ventes were \"pending capture\" (#929).\n\n**Cause.** No capture for those categories existed until #1091 (`R929a`-`R929d`).\n\n**Change.** Tests and docs only, no behaviour change.\n- `ForumListCompletionTests` now covers the 7 captured categories: the REST count (15, 7, 27, 10, 12, 10, 11), the page's links and order kept, the injected entries still at their legacy place; the client test makes one captured GET per category.\n- All 23 entries of `SubforumInjection` are checked in REST by title, and that count equals the table's size, so a new entry cannot go unchecked.\n- `docs/lots/LOT-168-forum-list-completeness.md`: pending capture section closed; `SubforumInjection` doc comment updated.\n\n**Tests.** `swift test` in `Packages/HFRKit`: 2120 tests pass; `swiftlint --strict` clean on the changed files. Mutation (« Win 9x/Me » renamed in the table): 4 named tests fail (`injectionsAgainstCapture`, `injectedCategories`, `completesEveryCapturedCategory`, `client`); reverted.\n\nNo gap row changes, so no `### Ledger`. No app code, so no `compile-check`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHiNaJQG4DNWwtL48n)_",
