   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-lot168-opus, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 255879a9\n\n1. **Medium**, `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:328`: §6b still says \"the entries of the other categories are not name-checked (pending capture)\". This PR does that check. Line 611 of the same file and the LOT-168 spec now say the opposite, so a reader of §6b gets the wrong answer (doc out of date, L08/L09). Fix: say the 23 entries were checked against `R285a`-`R285c` and `R929a`-`R929d` and are all in REST, apart from the dropped « PDA » and « Biblio Links ».\n2. **Low**, `ForumListCompletionTests.swift:85-103` (`injectedCategories`):\n   - The title says \"the page lists every REST row but the injected ones\", but no assertion checks it. `completed.count == rows.count` and the order check repeat `completesEveryCapturedCategory`.\n   - `pageKeys.contains(injected)` reads the page after the parser has already injected the entries, so it never compares them with REST.\n   - Fix: add `#expect(completed == home)` (my probe shows the page already equals REST, same order, for 14, 4, 12 and 6). Also check `rows` titles contain `want.injected`.\n3. **Detail**, `docs/lots/LOT-168-forum-list-completeness.md` §Limits: \"in a category not captured yet … That is why the capture below matters\" points to a \"Pending capture\" section that now says None. Reword it: every injected category is now captured.\n\nClaims checked against the captures:\n- REST counts are 10/12/10/11.\n- All 7 newly checked entries are in the REST names: Divers, Win 9x/Me, Concours, Ressources, Divers, Divers, Règles et coutumes.\n- The table holds 23 entries: Programmation 14, plus 1 + 1 + 7.\n- The meta URLs match the requests in the `client` test.\n\n**Verified**:\n- Ran `swift test --filter \"ForumListCompletionTests|ForumListParserTests\"` on 255879a9: 24 tests, all green.\n- Ran `swiftlint` on the 3 Swift files: clean.\n- Probe test printing page, REST and completed lists for cats 14/4/12/6: identical, nothing added.\n- Mutation 1, renaming the Photonumerique injected title: `injectionsAgainstCapture` fails at :139.\n- Mutation 2, deleting the Galerie-Perso injection: the tests fail.\n\nRound 1 fixed in fb91802 (all three findings; one commit).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
