   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-opus-lot168-r2, round 2): APPROVE** (head fb91802)\n\nThe PR changes tests and docs only. The source change is the `SubforumInjection` doc comment. The fixtures `R929a`-`R929d` and their MANIFEST rows were already on `dev-swift`, so the spec is right to say \"no new capture\". I found nothing blocking. Two wording details remain:\n\n1. **Detail**, `docs/lots/LOT-168-forum-list-completeness.md:19`: the spec says the four later categories' counts \"equal the page's list plus the REST rows it lacks\". `injectedCategories` asserts `completed == home`, so the page lacks no REST row there and that clause is empty. Fix: \"equal the page's list (injections included); REST adds nothing\".\n2. **Detail**, `docs/lots/LOT-168-forum-list-completeness.md:21` (Limits): \"an injected entry that HFR dropped, in REST later, would stay\" does not read as a sentence. Fix: \"an injected entry that HFR drops later would stay\".\n\n**Docs consistency.** I searched `docs/` and `Sources/HFRParsing/Lists` for \"pending capture\", \"not captured\", \"not name-check\" and \"unchecked\" next to \"injection\", \"table\", \"sub-forum\" or \"929\". Nothing is left: HFR-PROTOCOL §6b:328 and §6c:611 agree with the spec, and LOT-021:81 still holds. The count of 23 checks out: Hardware 1 (Bench) + Overclocking 1 + Programmation 14 + 7 = 23. This matches `SubforumInjection.all` and the test's new invariant line.\n\n**Titles vs assertions.** `injectedCategories` asserts what its title says: counts, injected titles on the page and in REST, and `completed == home`. The `client` test now covers 8 categories with counts `[15, 1, 7, 27, 10, 12, 10, 11]`.\n\n**Vérifié** (worktree at fb91802, removed afterwards):\n- `swift test --filter \"ForumListCompletion|ForumListParser\"`: 24/24 passed.\n- `swiftlint lint` on the touched dirs: clean.\n- Mutation: I deleted the « Win 9x/Me » row (`SubforumInjection.swift:41`). `injectionsAgainstCapture` then fails (22 ≠ 23), and `injectedCategories` fails twice (the page key is missing and `completed != home`). Change reverted.\n\nAuthor reply: the two details are optional wording (REVIEW-ROUNDS step 8): not pushed, so the APPROVE stays on fb91802; they go into the next push that touches the spec.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
